slml 0.2
@mistake{bg#fff4f2 p16 r10 g6 w:f}
@fix{bg#f0faf4 p16 r10 g6 w:f}
@label{b s13}

meta{"Why not HTML?" lang:en}

page{bg#f6f6f9 a:c
  c{w:f mw860 g20
    "[Back to the start page](index.slml)"
    #"Why not HTML?"
    t{c#5b5b66 s18 "HTML grew for thirty years without breaking old pages. SLML starts over and keeps the good ideas."}
    r{g12
      c.mistake{
        t.label{c#b42318 "HTML"}
        "Broken markup is silently \"fixed\" by complex error recovery; every browser must guess the same way."
      }
      c.fix{
        t.label{c#146c43 "SLML"}
        "A document is valid or rejected, with the exact line and a hint. Same input, same result."
      }
    }
    r{g12
      c.mistake{
        t.label{c#b42318 "HTML"}
        "Three languages (HTML, CSS, JS) with three syntaxes, plus selectors and cascade to connect them."
      }
      c.fix{
        t.label{c#146c43 "SLML"}
        "Structure and style use one grammar. Styles are named attribute sets applied directly."
      }
    }
    r{g12
      c.mistake{
        t.label{c#b42318 "HTML"}
        "Layout was added later: floats, tables, then flexbox and grid on top."
      }
      c.fix{
        t.label{c#146c43 "SLML"}
        "row, column, gap, fill and align are the layout model from day one."
      }
    }
    r{g12
      c.mistake{
        t.label{c#b42318 "HTML"}
        "Whitespace collapsing, entities like &amp;, optional closing tags, quirks mode."
      }
      c.fix{
        t.label{c#146c43 "SLML"}
        "Text is always quoted and literal. Escapes are \\n, \\\" and \\u{...}. A version line replaces doctype guessing."
      }
    }
    r{g12
      c.mistake{
        t.label{c#b42318 "HTML"}
        "Accessibility is optional: an image without alt is still valid."
      }
      c.fix{
        t.label{c#146c43 "SLML"}
        "image requires alt. Decorative images say so explicitly with alt: \"\"."
      }
    }
    |
    t{c#5b5b66 s14 "SLML is young. See `ROADMAP.md` for what comes next: components, grid, forms, networking and a WebAssembly playground."}
  }
}
